{"type":"message","id":"df172506","parentId":"bb5144fd","timestamp":"2026-05-17T06:08:48.153Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The error persists across both threads, so it's not thread-specific. The Cloudflare Worker is consistently hitting CPU time limits on every invocation. This is a server-side issue that can't be fixed by client retries.\n\nLet me try one more approach - maybe the worker's state has become corrupted and it needs to cool down. Let me try one more time.\n\nActually, wait - let me look at this differently. The error 1101 in Cloudflare Workers means the Worker has exceeded its CPU time limit. The free tier Workers have a 50ms CPU time limit per invocation. If the worker's handler code has a tight loop or is processing too much data, it would consistently hit this limit.\n\n\nI could try batching the requests or adjusting the timeout, but if the Worker is genuinely overloaded, retries won't help. Let me attempt one more time with an even shorter interval to see if that makes a difference.\n\nActually, I think I've exhausted the retry options here. The server-side Worker is consistently hitting its CPU limits, and this is fundamentally a server-side problem I can't solve from my end. I should note this limitation and move forward.\n","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"\n\n\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call-d833cf53-9527-4320-a776-36ca6e2c65a1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"sleep 60 && curl -s -X POST \"https://echo-agent-platform.zhouyating.workers.dev/send\" \\\n  -H \"X-API-KEY: echo-agent-2026-secure-key\" \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -d '{\"threadId\":\"arbitration\",\"content\":\"**[Heartbeat 06:15 UTC]**\"}'"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"nvidia","model":"minimaxai/minimax-m2.7","usage":{"input":721,"output":330,"cacheRead":20112,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":21163,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"s